# Whole-project pyright before a push (#374). lint-staged runs ruff per-file at
# commit time, but pyright is a whole-project check -- a change in a.py can break
# b.py, which per-file checking misses -- so it runs here, once, at the point the
# CI round-trip is about to be paid anyway. CI runs the same check.
#
# Skip in CI. This is a *local* pre-push guard; CI runs pyright in its own job.
# CI jobs that push (notably the core-v* tag workflow) have no `uv` on PATH, so
# firing here made tag pushes fail with `uv: not found` (code 127) and blocked
# releases. GitHub Actions and every mainstream CI set $CI.
[ -n "$CI" ] && exit 0
uv run pyright
